    <DataNode elementId="AT2G19070-MONOMER" textLabel="spermidine hydroxycinnamoyl transferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64470" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">At2G19070 was expressed in E. coli, purified and analyzed for enzyme activity |CITS: [19077165]|. The recombinant enzyme was shown to specifically acylate spermidine. Neither putrescine nor spermine were effectively acylated. Several hydroxycinnamoyl-CoAs were found to be effective acyl donors. Among them, feruloyl-CoA appeared to be the most preferred donor, followed by caffeoyl-CoA, coumaroyl-CoA and cinnamoyl-CoA. Sinapoyl-CoA was a poor acyl donor and hydroxyferuloyl-CoA was not accepted by the enzyme. At2G19070 is specifically expressed in the anther tapetum cell layers. It is transcriptionally regulated by MS1 (male sterile 1). Mutations in At2G19070 had an impact on pollen grain autofluorescence and pollen wall development |CITS: [19077165]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G19070-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G19070.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64470" />
